# BaseAuth

A production-ready, full-stack authentication boilerplate built for small to medium-sized projects. Drop it into any project that needs secure, battle-tested auth without reinventing the wheel — register, login, OTP-based email verification, password recovery, and full account management, all wired up and ready to extend.

## Why BaseAuth?

Most projects need the same auth flow: sign up, verify email, log in, manage your account, log out securely. Instead of rebuilding this from scratch (and re-making the same security mistakes) every time, BaseAuth gives you a boilerplate you can clone, configure, and ship.

## Features

- **Register** — new user sign-up with input validation
- **Email Verification (OTP)** — free OTP-based email verification on signup, no paid email service required
- **Login** — secure credential-based authentication
- **Forgot Password** — OTP/email-based password reset flow
- **Session Management** — refresh token rotation with reuse detection
- **Account Settings** (post-login):
  - Change name
  - Change email (re-verification via OTP)
  - Change password
  - Change phone number
  - Delete account
- **httpOnly Cookies** — access & refresh tokens never exposed to client-side JS
- **JWT Authentication** — short-lived access tokens + long-lived refresh tokens

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React (Vite) + TypeScript |
| State Management | Zustand |
| Routing | React Router v6 |
| Backend | Node.js + Express + TypeScript |
| Database | MongoDB (Mongoose) |
| Auth | JWT (access + refresh tokens), httpOnly cookies |
| Email/OTP | Nodemailer via Gmail (free, no paid email service required) |

